{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CLOSE HANG DIAGNOSIS. S3+S6 closes wedged 5h at 0.0%% CPU, state S (sleeping) - blocked, not computing; no per-ticket lock held; global .ticket-write.lock is a 0-byte flock sentinel. Most consistent with a hung network read to the completion verifier with no timeout. SYSTEMIC, not caused by my parallelism: another session's close (impl-obese-dihedral-ermine) is ALSO sleeping at 1h40m. Killed my two wedged procs; both tickets remained cleanly in_progress with no partial state. Also learned: 'nohup ... &' inside a timed Bash tool call does NOT survive the tool timeout killing the process group - must use the harness run_in_background mode. Switching to SEQUENTIAL closes (they serialize on the store write lock anyway, so concurrency bought nothing). S4 also needs a re-review first: widening its file_impact 9->15 paths (to declare criterion-pins.json and the folded-in guide files) staled its attestation - the gate correctly caught both that the commit touched undeclared files AND that fixing the declaration invalidated the review."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787229539965318001,"uuid":"0732933f-0516-4a1a-bf48-95daf8c50e1e"}